@startuml Reset Password Sequence Diagram
title UC06 - Reset Password (Verify OTP)

actor "User" as User
boundary "Reset Password Page" as Frontend
participant ":authRoutes" as Routes
participant ":authController" as Controller
participant ":authService" as Service
participant ":OTP Model" as OTPModel
participant ":User Model" as UserModel
database ":MongoDB" as DB

ref over User, Frontend, Routes, Controller, Service, OTPModel, UserModel, DB
  UC05 - Forgot Password (Send OTP)
  User requests password reset and OTP is sent to email
end ref

User -> Frontend: 1. Enter OTP and new password
activate Frontend

Frontend -> Frontend: 2. validateFields()

opt [Validation failed]
    Frontend --> User: 2.1 Display error
end

Frontend -> Routes: 3. POST /api/auth/reset-password\n(email, otp, newPassword)
activate Routes

Routes -> Controller: 4. resetPassword(req, res)
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: 5. resetPassword(email, otp, newPassword)
activate Service

Service -> OTPModel: 6. findOne({email, otp})
activate OTPModel

OTPModel -> DB: 7. Query OTP
activate DB

DB --> OTPModel: 8. OTP document or null
deactivate DB

OTPModel --> Service: 9. OTP data
deactivate OTPModel

opt [Invalid OTP]
    Service --> Controller: 10.1 AppError "Invalid OTP code" 400
    deactivate Service
    Controller --> Routes: 10.2 HTTP 400 Response
    deactivate Controller
    Routes --> Frontend: 10.3 JSON Error
    deactivate Routes
    Frontend --> User: 10.4 Display error
end

Service -> Service: 10. Check OTP expiresAt

opt [OTP expired]
    Service --> Controller: 11.1 AppError "OTP has expired" 400
    deactivate Service
    Controller --> Routes: 11.2 HTTP 400 Response
    deactivate Controller
    Routes --> Frontend: 11.3 JSON Error
    deactivate Routes
    Frontend --> User: 11.4 Display error
end

Service -> Service: 11. Hash newPassword

Service -> UserModel: 12. findOneAndUpdate({email}, {password})
activate UserModel

UserModel -> DB: 13. Update password
activate DB

DB --> UserModel: 14. Updated user
deactivate DB

UserModel --> Service: 15. User data
deactivate UserModel

Service -> OTPModel: 16. deleteOne({email, otp})
activate OTPModel

OTPModel -> DB: 17. Delete used OTP
activate DB

DB --> OTPModel: 18. Deleted
deactivate DB

OTPModel --> Service: 19. Success
deactivate OTPModel

Service --> Controller: 20. Return success message
deactivate Service

Controller --> Routes: 21. HTTP 200 Response
deactivate Controller

Routes --> Frontend: 22. JSON {message: "Password changed successfully"}
deactivate Routes

Frontend --> User: 23. Display message and redirect to login page
deactivate Frontend

@enduml
